<title>USA: Missouri jobless rate drops to 3.6 percent in Sept.</title>
<headline>Missouri jobless rate drops to 3.6 percent in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The September unemployment rate in Missouri fell to 3.6 percent from 4.3 percent in August, the state's department of labor and industrial relations reported Thursday.</p>
<p>The 3.6 percent jobless rate for September ties with May 1979 as being the lowest rate in the state since 1978, the department said.</p>
<p>The report estimated that 101,500 people were unemployed in Missouri last month, compared to 122,000 in August. The state's September 1995 jobless rate was 4.4 percent.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
</text>
